# AI Secretary — Chat Memory & Context Update

The goal is to give the AI the ability to remember previous messages in a conversation. This is essential for natural follow-up questions like "Summarize it" or "Tell me more about that email".

## Proposed Changes

### [Memory Layer]

#### [MODIFY] [orchestrator.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py)
*   Add `self.memory = {}` to track message history per `chat_id`.
*   Maintain a rolling window of the last 10 messages to keep the context relevant and tokens low.
*   Integrate history into the [_agent_loop](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py#233-295) so the AI sees the full conversation.

#### [MODIFY] [tools/agent_tracer.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/agent_tracer.py)
*   Ensure traces reflect the inclusion of chat history.

## Vector Store Consideration
For "Long-term" memory (remembering things from weeks ago), we could add a **Vector Database** (e.g., ChromaDB). This would allow the AI to search through an infinite library of past interactions.
> [!NOTE]
> I will start with **Short-term Memory** (last 10 messages) first, as it's the most impactful for day-to-day chatting.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
*   Send a message to the bot: "What was the last email about?"
*   Follow up with: "Summarize it in 2 bullet points." 
*   If the AI knows what "it" refers to, the memory is working.
